{
  "case_id": "2024-24-320",
  "document_hash": "5562cf6cd09385c8179644f828094b21cf14dc1ee9ff727ba7615e3bc90b02d5",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2024-24-320",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5562cf6cd09385c8179644f828094b21cf14dc1ee9ff727ba7615e3bc90b02d5",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5562cf6cd093-0000-0000",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 2,
        "start": 2
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The above-entitled matter came on for oral argument before the Supreme Court of the United States at 11:32 a.m."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2024-24-320",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5562cf6cd09385c8179644f828094b21cf14dc1ee9ff727ba7615e3bc90b02d5",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5562cf6cd093-0000-0001",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 2,
        "start": 2
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "APPEARANCES: TACY F. FLINT, ESQUIRE, Chicago, Illinois; on behalf of the Petitioner. CAROLINE A. FLYNN, Assistant to the Solicitor General, Department of Justice, Washington, D.C.; on behalf of the Respondent."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2024-24-320",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5562cf6cd09385c8179644f828094b21cf14dc1ee9ff727ba7615e3bc90b02d5",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5562cf6cd093-0000-0008",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "This case starts and ends with the text of the Combat-Related Special Compensation statute. Because that statute grants the secretary concerned authority to settle claims for CRSC, the Barring Act does not apply."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2024-24-320",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5562cf6cd09385c8179644f828094b21cf14dc1ee9ff727ba7615e3bc90b02d5",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5562cf6cd093-0000-0009",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 5
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The CRSC statute does that. Start with subsection (d). It provides for the secretary of a military department to consider whether a veteran is eligible for CRSC using CRSC-specific procedures and criteria. Because subsection (d) authorizes the secretary to consider whether a veteran is eligible for CRSC, it authorizes a specific government official to determine whether the claim is valid."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Thomas",
      "case_id": "2024-24-320",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5562cf6cd09385c8179644f828094b21cf14dc1ee9ff727ba7615e3bc90b02d5",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5562cf6cd093-0000-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 6,
        "start": 6
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "And yet the government argues that if we agree with you, there would be a considerable number of other statutes that would confer settlement -- settlement authority."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Government",
      "case_id": "2024-24-320",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5562cf6cd09385c8179644f828094b21cf14dc1ee9ff727ba7615e3bc90b02d5",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5562cf6cd093-0000-0011",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 9,
        "start": 9
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "none of these statutes are part of this case because the government's theory is that the Court should not read Section 1413a literally because of the risk that these other statutes will create a destabilization in their terms of military pay."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2024-24-320",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5562cf6cd09385c8179644f828094b21cf14dc1ee9ff727ba7615e3bc90b02d5",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5562cf6cd093-0000-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 15,
        "start": 15
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "What is it?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kavanaugh",
      "case_id": "2024-24-320",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5562cf6cd09385c8179644f828094b21cf14dc1ee9ff727ba7615e3bc90b02d5",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5562cf6cd093-0000-0006",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 17,
        "start": 17
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "What should we make of the waiver provision?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2024-24-320",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5562cf6cd09385c8179644f828094b21cf14dc1ee9ff727ba7615e3bc90b02d5",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5562cf6cd093-0000-0015",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 18,
        "start": 18
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "the waiver provision doesn't come into play."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2024-24-320",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5562cf6cd09385c8179644f828094b21cf14dc1ee9ff727ba7615e3bc90b02d5",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5562cf6cd093-0000-0007",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 23,
        "start": 23
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "What about the situation where -- the situation where the veteran owes a lot of money to the government?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Gorsuch",
      "case_id": "2024-24-320",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5562cf6cd09385c8179644f828094b21cf14dc1ee9ff727ba7615e3bc90b02d5",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5562cf6cd093-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 24,
        "start": 24
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "In your understanding of the statute, who does the offsets? How are they accounted for?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Gorsuch",
      "case_id": "2024-24-320",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5562cf6cd09385c8179644f828094b21cf14dc1ee9ff727ba7615e3bc90b02d5",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5562cf6cd093-0001-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 25,
        "start": 25
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "All right. But -- but 2, the -- the $500 that the --the veteran happens to owe the department for whatever reason, who does that and how before the secretary of the relevant military department is authorized to pay?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2024-24-320",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5562cf6cd09385c8179644f828094b21cf14dc1ee9ff727ba7615e3bc90b02d5",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5562cf6cd093-0001-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 26,
        "start": 26
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "All -- all -- all of the offsets have been imposed by regulatory direction, correct?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Jackson",
      "case_id": "2024-24-320",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5562cf6cd09385c8179644f828094b21cf14dc1ee9ff727ba7615e3bc90b02d5",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5562cf6cd093-0001-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 27,
        "start": 27
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "In the Barring Act, when there's a six-year statute of limitations, do we know from when it accrues, or does it work backwards from the person's application?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kavanaugh",
      "case_id": "2024-24-320",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5562cf6cd09385c8179644f828094b21cf14dc1ee9ff727ba7615e3bc90b02d5",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5562cf6cd093-0001-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 34,
        "start": 34
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "So, on page 34 of the government's brief, they say that other than this case and one other federal claims case, there's no comptroller general, Department of Defense, or judicial decision that finds section 3702(b)(1)'s limitations period inapplicable to any form of military compensation in Title 10 or Title 37. I just want to -- is that accurate?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2024-24-320",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5562cf6cd09385c8179644f828094b21cf14dc1ee9ff727ba7615e3bc90b02d5",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5562cf6cd093-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 47,
        "start": 47
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: Counsel, what -- what is the concern you have broader beyond -- beyond this particular statute? I mean, to be eligible for benefits here, you have to have gotten a Purple Heart, be disabled as a result of armed conflict, hazardous service, performance of duty under conditions of war."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Gorsuch",
      "case_id": "2024-24-320",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5562cf6cd09385c8179644f828094b21cf14dc1ee9ff727ba7615e3bc90b02d5",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5562cf6cd093-0002-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 50,
        "start": 50
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GORSUCH: I want to hear what the six are and do all of them contain statutes of limitations, or are some of them lack them too?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kavanaugh",
      "case_id": "2024-24-320",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5562cf6cd09385c8179644f828094b21cf14dc1ee9ff727ba7615e3bc90b02d5",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5562cf6cd093-0003-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 67,
        "start": 67
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAVANAUGH: -- what's the relevance of that? Would you summarize that for us?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Government",
      "case_id": "2024-24-320",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5562cf6cd09385c8179644f828094b21cf14dc1ee9ff727ba7615e3bc90b02d5",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5562cf6cd093-0003-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 68,
        "start": 68
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "So it's that -- the GAO was the one sort of implementing the statute for a long time, and the comptroller general decisions are what we have as authorities in this area of what counts."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kavanaugh",
      "case_id": "2024-24-320",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5562cf6cd09385c8179644f828094b21cf14dc1ee9ff727ba7615e3bc90b02d5",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5562cf6cd093-0003-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 69,
        "start": 69
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAVANAUGH: And the other point, there's no other form of military compensation where the limitations period is inapplicable, correct?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2024-24-320",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5562cf6cd09385c8179644f828094b21cf14dc1ee9ff727ba7615e3bc90b02d5",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5562cf6cd093-0003-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 70,
        "start": 70
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "to be the word \"settle,\" but it has to be a hallmark formulation. And then my friend read examples of words that, in the government's view, sound \"hallmark\" enough."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Government",
      "case_id": "2024-24-320",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5562cf6cd09385c8179644f828094b21cf14dc1ee9ff727ba7615e3bc90b02d5",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5562cf6cd093-0003-0005",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 72,
        "start": 72
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "A statute that authorizes an official to determine the validity and amount due on claims is a statute that authorizes settlement."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2024-24-320",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5562cf6cd09385c8179644f828094b21cf14dc1ee9ff727ba7615e3bc90b02d5",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5562cf6cd093-0003-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 74,
        "start": 74
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: Thank you, counsel. The case is submitted."
    },
    {
